{{also|DINK}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪŋk/}}
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 dink.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪŋk|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
Imitative. Originally {{w|United States|US}}. Attested since the 1930s.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|tennis}} A soft [[drop shot]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2018|author=Ava Wallace|title=New mother Serena Williams returns to tennis, with a little rust and plenty to learn|journal=Washington Post|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/sports/tennis/new-mother-serena-williams-returns-to-tennis-with-a-little-rust-and-plenty-to-learn/2018/02/12/2cbb4404-1012-11e8-9065-e55346f6de81_story.html|text=But what I saw is she still has that sense of, ‘Okay, I need to hit a '''dink''' shot, I need to come with power now, I need to change up my serve not for a flat one, but a big kick.’|month=February 12}}
# {{lb|en|[[pickleball]]}} A soft drop shot played at or near the non-volley zone.
# {{lb|en|soccer}} A light [[chip]]; a [[chip]]ped pass or shot
#*{{quote-journal|en|date=29 April 2021|author=Jamie Jackson|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2021/apr/29/manchester-united-roma-europa-league-semi-final-first-leg-match-report|work=The Guardian|title=Edinson Cavani and Bruno Fernandes help Manchester United hit Roma for six|passage=The forward passed to Fernandes and, as Pau López advanced, the Portuguese fashioned a sand‑wedge '''dink''' over the goalkeeper.}}

=====Translations=====
{{trans-top|sports}}
* Dutch: {{t+|nl|lobben}}
{{trans-bottom}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|tennis}} To play a soft drop shot.
# (''[[pickleball]]'') To play a soft drop shot at or near the non-volley zone.
# {{lb|en|football}} To [[chip]] lightly, to play a light [[chip]] shot.
#: ''The forward '''dinked''' the ball over the goalkeeper to score his first goal of the season.''
#* {{quote-web
|en
|date=December 28, 2010
|author=Kevin Darlin
|title=West Brom 1 - 3 Blackburn
|work=BBC
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9308862.stm
|page=
|passage=But the visitors started the game in stunning fashion when Morten Gamst Pedersen '''dinked''' forward a clever looping pass and Kalinic beat the offside trap, surged into the box and beautifully placed the ball past goalkeeper Scott Carson.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=7 Jan 2024|author=Gary Rose|title=Manchester City 5-0 Huddersfield Town|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67895100|work=BBC Sport|passage=A '''dinked''' pass intended for De Bruyne from the impressive Oscar Bobb then deflected off Jackson and looped into the net early in the second half before Foden smashed in his second.}}

===Etymology 2===
{{unknown|en|title=Origin unknown}}. Attested since the 1930s.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Australia|colloquial}} A ride on the crossbar or handlebars of a bicycle.
#: ''I gave him a '''dink''' on my bike.''

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|Australia|colloquial}} To carry someone on a pushbike: behind, on the crossbar or on the handlebar.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1947|editor=w:John Lehmann|journal=The Penguin New Writing|issue=30|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=z9EzAAAAMAAJ&q=dink|page=103
|passage=I didn't like them at all ; only the lame one who used to let me '''dink''' him home on his bicycle.}}

